---
import { ecosystem } from '../../data/portfolio.js';
---
<section class="slide soft" id="ecosystem" data-section>
  <div class="slide-canvas"><div class="canvas-inner">
    <div class="section-head"><span class="section-kicker">02 · Product Ecosystem</span><h2>Product connects the enterprise system.</h2><p>Business, customer, product, technology, data, operations, automation, AI and compliance work as one operating model.</p></div>
    <div class="ecosystem-layout">
      <article class="dark-story"><span class="story-index">PRODUCT ECOSYSTEM</span><h3>One product lens.<br />Multiple enterprise realities.</h3><p>I translate business goals into journeys, capabilities, workflows, data models, integrations and measurable outcomes.</p><div class="story-points"><span>Customer value</span><span>Business economics</span><span>Technology feasibility</span><span>Operational control</span></div></article>
      <div class="ecosystem-grid">
        {ecosystem.map(([title, text, tags], index) => <article class={`eco-card eco-${index + 1}`}><span class="card-number">0{index + 1}</span><h3>{title}</h3><p>{text}</p><small>{tags}</small></article>)}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div></div>
</section>
